OMS Rules — Protected
Canonical lifecycle
SCANNED → CANDIDATE → QUALIFIED → RISK_CHECK → ORDER_PENDING → PARTIALLY_FILLED → FILLED → MANAGED → SCALE_OUT → EXIT → CLOSED
Rules
Every order intent gets an idempotency key.
Internal order ID is separate from broker order ID.
Broker events must be reconciled into internal state.
Partial fills are first-class.
Rejections/cancellations are first-class events.
Position state is derived from authoritative fills plus reconciliation.
Never infer a fill only from UI state.
Never place a broker order directly from frontend code.
